Description: Fix CVE-2026-73231 — block eval injection in helpers.fake()
 The fake() template resolver walked attacker-controlled dotted method
 paths by blindly dereferencing each part along the prototype chain
 (currentModuleOrMethod?.[part]). A template such as
 {{test.constructor("<js>")}} could therefore resolve the JavaScript
 Function constructor and lead to arbitrary code execution (Eval
 Injection, CWE-94). This adds a guard that refuses to traverse into the
 dangerous prototype-chain properties constructor, __proto__ and
 prototype, throwing the existing FakerError instead. Legitimate
 module.method lookups (e.g. name.firstName, phone.number) are
 unaffected.
 .
 Retargeted at the compiled bundles shipped in the npm registry tarball
 (dist/cjs/modules/helpers/index.js and the dist/esm helpers chunk), since
 the @faker-js/faker 7.6.0 npm package ships only compiled dist/ output and
 contains no src/*.ts. The upstream fix (PR #3852, v10.5.0) targets
 src/modules/helpers/eval.ts, which does not exist in this version.
 .
 The pristine 7.6.0 tarball declares "types": "index.d.ts" in package.json
 but does not ship that root file (it is normally emitted by the upstream
 build:types step). The native universal builder installs with --omit=dev,
 so npm-run-all (run-s) is absent and the build cannot regenerate it, which
 fails the entry-point validator. This patch adds the missing root
 index.d.ts (re-exporting dist/types) and lists it in package.json "files"
 so the repacked tarball satisfies its own declared entry point.
Origin: ai-synthesized, CVE-2026-73231
Author: Root.io Novel Patcher <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-09-03

--- /dev/null
+++ b/index.d.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+// Root type-declaration entry point (package.json "types": "index.d.ts").
+// Re-exports the shipped compiled declarations under dist/types. Regenerated
+// as part of CVE-2026-73231 so the published dist-only tarball satisfies its
+// own declared entry point without requiring a full devDependency build.
+export * from './dist/types/index';
